# =============================================================================
# CitOmni - robots.txt (STAGING)
#
# PURPOSE
#   Allow compliant crawlers to fetch staging responses so they can observe the
#   HTTP noindex policy, while keeping staging accessible to reviewers and clients.
#
# THREAT MODEL
#   - Prevent staging URLs and duplicate/incomplete content from being indexed.
#   - Avoid blocking crawlers before they can observe the X-Robots-Tag noindex header.
#
# BEHAVIOR
#   - The empty "Disallow" rule imposes no crawl restriction.
#   - Staging responses send X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive.
#
# NOINDEX
#   - Do not add "Noindex:" here. It is not a supported robots.txt directive.
#   - Do not use "Disallow: /" for staging: a blocked crawler cannot fetch the
#     response that carries the authoritative X-Robots-Tag noindex directive.
#   - robots.txt controls crawling; the HTTP X-Robots-Tag controls indexing.
#
# NOTES
#   - Staging is intentionally reachable for review and testing.
#   - mod_headers must be enabled so the staging .htaccess files can emit the
#     X-Robots-Tag noindex header.
# =============================================================================


User-agent: *
Disallow:
